                <pb facs="1242" n="1228" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg1228"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00116 European War 1939/1241: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Harrison</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-01-13T20:00:00-04:00">January 13, 1944—8
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>126. Department would be grateful if Swiss representatives protecting our
                    interests in Germany would follow the matter discussed in your 216, January 10,
                    7 p.m. attentively and desires you to keep Department promptly informed of
                    developments.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
